    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it's more about a natural inclination toward tradition over progress. Some of the other texts I've read for this seminar suggest that many officials in your position actually viewed the local population as being quite primitive or even incapable of higher reasoning compared to Europeans. From your position of authority, how much weight do you actually give to those views? Would you say there's a natural hierarchy at play here?",
